{
  "id": "s03-l02",
  "unit": "s03-vowel-signs",
  "title": "Vowel signs 2: ু ূ ৃ",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "These three signs hang **below** the consonant.\n\n**ু** (`u`) and **ূ** (`u`): ফুফু (`fufu`), খালু (`khalu`), আপু (`apu`), দূরে (`dure`, *far*). Like ি/ী they sound the same; the long-u sign has an extra loop.\n\n**Shape changes**: after a few letters the sign joins in a new way. **রু** and **রূ** attach to the side of র; **হু** gets a curl and **হৃ** a hook; **শু** and **গু** fold the sign into the letter. You'll recognize them with practice; when in doubt, look for the base letter first.\n\n**ৃ** is the sign form of ঋ and says `ri`: কৃষক (`krishok`, *farmer*), পৃথিবী (`prithibi`, *world*).",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "k-u",
      "bn": "কু",
      "tr": "ku",
      "en": "ু (u-kar, short-u sign): adds 'u' as in 'food'",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ু (U+09C1), name hroshsho u-kar (হ্রস্ব উ-কার). Below the letter; joins differently after র, হ, শ, গ (রু, হু, শু, গু). Same sound as ূ."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-uu",
      "bn": "কূ",
      "tr": "ku",
      "en": "ূ (long-u sign): adds 'u' as in 'food'",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ূ (U+09C2), name dirgho u-kar (দীর্ঘ উ-কার). Same sound as ু. After র it becomes রূ."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-ri",
      "bn": "কৃ",
      "tr": "kri",
      "en": "ৃ (ri-kar): adds 'ri' as in 'rip'",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ৃ (U+09C3), name ri-kar (ঋ-কার). The sign form of ঋ. After হ it looks like হৃ."
    },
    {
      "id": "krishok",
      "bn": "কৃষক",
      "tr": "krishok",
      "en": "farmer"
    },
    {
      "id": "prithibi",
      "bn": "পৃথিবী",
      "tr": "prithibi",
      "en": "world / Earth"
    }
  ],
